WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:04.940
Early summer... A time when
the temperature gradually increases,

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.490
and more students start to wear short sleeves.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:13.820
It was then that all of Attack Junior High
was hit by a different source of tension.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:18.040
A certain event was about to occur—
One that affects students in all grades.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:20.750
All the students' fates hung in the balance.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.460
If your name is called, come forward.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:28.460
Those idiots who failed the tests
will take makeup tests next week.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.340
Test Results
Makeup Test
for Failures

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.340
Keep that in mind.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:36.010
That event was the return of the test results.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:06.440
Year 1,      Class 4

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.770
Next, Armin Arlelt!

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.190
Yes, sir!

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:09.400
Period 5
Studying Hard! Titan Junior High School

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.150
Perfect score!

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:10.360
Period 5
Studying Hard! Titan Junior High School

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.190
Whoa!

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.280
Next, Sasha Braus!

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:15.780
<b>Year-1 Math,
First-Term Mid-Term
Exam Answer Sheet
Name: Sasha</b>

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.740
Yes, sir.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:16.950
<b>Year-1 Math,</b>

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.490
Hey, you...

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:22.080
What do you think you're doing?

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:35.630
I'm talking to <i>you</i>!
What the hell are you doing?!

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.520
If anything, I'd like to hear <i>your</i> trick...

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.940
...for staying sane
after flunking every subject.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:49.940
Indeed.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.770
Your scores were all
big fat zeros, weren't they?

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.690
But being told no lunch for you
if you flunked the makeup tests

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.820
freaked you out even more than the fact
that you flunked all the tests, didn't it?

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.160
Eren, please!

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.750
Stay and help me study!

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.080
Sorry, but I gotta go to the
Scouts room now, so... See ya!

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:09.670
- Mika—

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:10.750
- Eren, wait for me.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:12.340
Yeah, of course.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.670
Ah, you can go, Jean. You're a jerk, so...

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.420
You didn't have to tell me that!

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.800
- Argh! Who else could stay and help me study?!

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.510
- Uhm... Sasha?

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.760
If you want me to, I can—

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.770
As things stand, I'm gonna be lunchless!

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.850
Oh, all right, fine then.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.940
I can teach you the trick,
but unfortunately for you, I'm gifted.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.270
So all I can tell you is to "feel" it.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.780
You got all zeros, didn't you?

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.280
Oh, that's right!

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:39.450
Armin!

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.280
Please help me study!

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.620
For the makeup tests? Sure, I'll help you.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:44.780
Really?!

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:48.080
Sure, if I can be of help.
Would you like to study with us, too, Conny?

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:48.960
Is it okay?

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.000
I feel confident with you teaching us!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.840
Okay, then! Let's show what we can do
when we put our minds to it!

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.260
Yeah! Let's study hard together,
the three of us!

00:03:58.470 --> 00:03:59.630
Yeah!

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:00.720
- I'll do it!

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:01.050
- I'll do my best!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.930
- I'll do my best!
- If you guys try hard, you can do it!

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.310
Well then, let's start, shall we?

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.270
Huh?

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:12.810
Where's Conny?

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.770
Where the heck did he go?

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:22.160
Don't tell me... he forgot
about it and went home...

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.320
Summer has come in earnest.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:29.910
Well, let's not worry about Conny for now
and start with your weakest subject.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:30.960
Okay!

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:31.500
I'm very weak at math.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.380
<b>Class: 1-4
Name:  Sasha
Year-1 Math, First-Term Mid-Term Exam Answer Sheet</b>

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:34.580
<b>Year-1 Math, First-Term Mid-Term Exam Answer Sheet
Name:  Sasha
Class: 1-4</b>

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.420
Hmm... Let's see...

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:41.170
For example, for this formula with
X and Y, it'd be easier to understand

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.220
if you replace X with an apple
and Y with an orange.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:44.890
What?!

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.470
It might be easier to memorize it

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.140
if you think of it as a formula
to figure out food prices.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.140
X is an apple. Y is an orange.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.980
Doesn't this seem more relatable
to you now and make it seem less difficult?

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:01.150
Whoa! It might be working pretty good.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.700
So does that mean that just to figure out
the prices for an apple and an orange,

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:09.370
we're restrained, scolded
and even forced to take tests?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:13.710
What?! Why are you going back to
reality just for that part? That's not true!

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.590
X and Y have infinite possibilities!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.880
Infinite possibilities? Such as...?

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.880
F-For example,

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.800
you can indulge yourself in luxury
by having X as steak and Y as curry!

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:29.430
Whoa! Then, X can be broiled eel
on rice and Y can be a pickled plum?!

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:30.140
Right!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.390
X can be tempura and Y can be watermelon?!

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.640
That's right!

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.690
I didn't realize that math
is a subject that's full of dreams!

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.530
That's right! Math is wonderful!

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.570
Though not quite the way you're thinking.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:45.910
Okay! I'll try solving
the problem using this method!

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:49.240
Yeah! Give it a shot!
I'm sure you can do it, Sasha!

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:53.290
Ah, but you should avoid eating the
food combinations you mentioned earlier.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:54.500
Huh?

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:02.090
All right! The Scouts!
I'm gonna go to the Scouts' activities!

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.760
Don't run like that!

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.590
Good afternoon!

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.850
Oh. Hi, Year 1 guys. Welcome.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:10.930
Argh! Crap!

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:14.770
What am I gonna do?!
I never thought this would happen!

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.100
Seriously...! Enough griping already!

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.610
Did something happen?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:19.270
No, don't!

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:22.400
Oh, since you asked, I guess I have no choice

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.610
but to accede to your demands and explain.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.570
Tsk.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.660
The thing is, I didn't do well
on the tests we just took.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:29.660
No one asked.

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:33.370
That's the cause of my distress.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.170
Don't get cocky, rookies!

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.040
Come again?!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.670
At a time like this,
you should show your respect an—

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.300
Hey... Are you okay?

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:49.220
First impressions are important.
Those rookies are scared stiff, aren't they?

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.850
They're just dumbfounded.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:54.680
Humph! Whatever the case,
it went exactly as I planned.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:58.310
Hey, you didn't used
to talk like that, you know.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:03.020
If, by some chance...
you're trying to imitate Levi,

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.280
could you cut it out?

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:09.110
You're nothing like him at all, actually.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.490
Are you trying to nag me, Petra?

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:16.790
If you wanna act like you're my girlfriend,
there's more you need to do first...

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.330
I wish you <i>had</i> bitten your tongue off and died.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.550
Oh, come on. There's nothing wrong
with test scores being a bit lower, right?

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:28.340
Geez... I'm not talking about
something as superficial as test scores.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:32.970
I'm ashamed that I let my guard down
because I always get a perfect score.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:36.020
Well, I guess you guys wouldn't get it.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.600
And why do you think you wouldn't get it?

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:42.480
That's because you guys
haven't reached my level.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.690
I don't study at all, and yet, I always
get a perfect score for some reason.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.320
I can't help it.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:48.570
This guy is...

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.820
Hey... Are you still trying to imitate Levi?

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.870
I really want you to cut it out.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:56.370
You pretend that you don't study much, Oruo,

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.080
but your mom told me that
you stay up half the night

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.210
frantically studying before each test.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:04.420
Oruo, I brought you a
late-night snack. Have some.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.460
Your mom bragged to me, too, saying,

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:10.380
"My son Oruo studies very hard," the other day.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:14.350
Y-You guys want to know my scores that badly?!

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:18.480
Like I said, I got really bad scores, this time!

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:20.560
What?! You wanna see them no matter what?!

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.230
Like I said, no one asked.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:25.400
Humph! How can I fight against such enthusiasm?

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.900
If you insist that much,
I'll show my results to you.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.200
But you guys should show yours, too, okay?!

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.240
What?

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.120
Why is this happening?

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:37.290
Geez... I guess we just have to.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.120
One, two...

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:40.460
<b>Class: 2-3
Name: Oruo
Year-2 Math, First-Term Mid-Term Exam Answer Sheet</b>

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:41.750
What?!

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.920
You said bad... This score's bad?!

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:47.880
Ahh... I missed a <i>whopping</i> 6 points!

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:51.090
The Year 1 tests are so much easier
than Year 2's that it's not even funny.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.430
And given how you guys did,
you probably can't help me.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:55.680
I guess I'll ask the teacher.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:58.810
You just wanted to brag from the start!

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:03.850
Levi!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:04.940
Ta-da!

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:05.100
<b>Class: 3-1
Name: Hange
Year-3 Math, First-Term Mid-Term Exam Answer Sheet</b>

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:05.310
<b>Year-3 Math, First-Term Mid-Term Exam Answer Sheet
Name: Hange
Class: 3-1</b>

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:09.440
How about the one who did better
treats the other to <i>yakisoba</i> bread?

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:09.570
<b>Name: Levi
Year-3 Math, First-Term Mid-Term Exam Answer Sheet</b>

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:09.780
<b>Year-3 Math, First-Term Mid-Term Exam Answer Sheet
Name: Levi</b>

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:10.440
Shut up.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:10.650
<b>Year-3 Math, First-Term Mid-Term Exam Answer Sheet
Name: Levi</b>

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.990
What?!

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.950
Just kidding! I was just joking!

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.370
Levi! There's something
I need to talk to you about.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.700
I am very hungry right now.

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:23.120
And all I have in my wallet is 21 yen!

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:27.790
How's that?! You can't overcome
the guilt of not treating your poor friend,

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:28.920
now, can you?

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.920
Just eat Sacchan Squid or something.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.170
What?!

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:36.300
What're you saying?!
That's a squid! It's not bread!

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:40.270
Don't try and dodge the issue
by making a stupid comment like that!

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.640
So first you suggested a bet
when you already knew your score.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.940
Then you get on my case for
making an alternative suggestion?!

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:49.020
Has your brain become crap, too?

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:52.940
It's true... that my act of trying
to force you to buy me <i>yakisoba</i> bread

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.700
by any means necessary might've been beyond low.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:57.910
But...!

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:03.450
But... I'm going to do it.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.670
Starve to death.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.010
Okay, then! I'm gonna go leech
our underclassmen using your name!

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.340
You stupid Levi! Clipped hair!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.510
Don't use my name!

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:20.640
Geez...

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.900
What the hell are you guys doing?

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:31.860
Hange suddenly showed up and started
going on a rampage. It was terrible!

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:33.860
Levi! Please take Hange with you!

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.070
No thanks.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:39.030
Because of Hange's body splash, Oruo went down!

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.280
Not my problem.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:46.080
Levi, do you get now how serious I am?

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.580
Yeah, I get how seriously crap your brain is.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:54.880
Why are you short on money
like that in the first place?

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.720
Hey, stop! Don't ask that!

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.970
Ah... I knew it...

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:03.060
I <i>thought</i> you might be curious enough to ask...

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.390
Huh? Huh?!

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.430
...about...

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:10.270
...the most exciting stuff!

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:16.360
Hange, what'd you bring us
to the science room for?

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:20.110
Yeah. We, the Biology Club,
borrow the Science preparation room

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:21.740
and do activities in there.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.450
Welcome to the Biology Club.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:30.290
Huh? Hange! It's pitch dark in here.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:33.750
Let me introduce them to you!

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.170
T-Titans?!

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:36.880
Aren't they cute?

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:42.300
I'm going to name them after a bug and crab

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.720
I used to take care of a long time ago.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:48.100
Here we go again. <i>Another</i> one
of these naming ceremonies.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:49.690
You're "Sawney."

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.770
You're "Beane."

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.440
Let's all be friends!

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.570
Hange! You're too close!

00:11:56.980 --> 00:11:58.780
Whoa! That was close!

00:11:58.990 --> 00:12:00.320
That's dangerous, Hange!

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.120
It's impossible to keep Titans!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.830
That's not true!

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:08.290
I want to try to view the Titans from
a different angle than the existing one

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.620
by taking care of Titans!

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:13.460
It might end as a waste of time,

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:16.880
but... I'm going to do it.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.220
Hmm? What?

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.010
What is it?!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:25.970
Whoa!

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.970
Hange! Please step back!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.480
Almost got me that time, Sawney!

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:34.270
You're seriously gonna die!

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:37.150
I see...

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.150
So this is the reason why you're broke.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.150
Levi!

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:43.030
That's right! Because the cost
of their food is so enormous,

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.870
our club budget is always in the red.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:48.950
And using my allowance
isn't helping at all, either.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.330
I guess it can't be helped.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:56.630
Levi...

00:12:56.840 --> 00:13:00.470
I'm not treating you.
Make sure you repay me later.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:03.720
Levi!

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:04.930
Here.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:06.180
Headlong Dog Food

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:07.180
What's this?

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:08.810
The food for the Titans, of course.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:09.770
It's not for Hange?!

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:13.390
You go buy Sacchan Squid
with that 21 yen and eat it.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.770
Geez... He's a stubborn one.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:24.280
That's great, Sasha!
You got most of them correct!

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.820
That's because you're a good teacher.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:31.200
No, this is without doubt your own ability.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:34.870
My impression of Armin was that he's just weak,

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.880
but he's very kind and smart.

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:40.920
He's got lots of wonderful traits.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.640
Armin, thank you very much for your help today.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:49.890
Yep. Good luck with your makeup tests.
I'll see you tomorrow! See ya!

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:56.520
You helped me study, Armin.
I'll do my best on tomorrow's makeup for you!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:57.730
Okay!

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:02.990
Hm?

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:07.570
It's dark on the street!

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:08.530
What's wrong?!

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:11.660
I'm scared of the dark! I'm scared of the dark!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.790
I guess he <i>is</i> weak after all.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:23.960
I'll give you, who are lesser
than livestock, the makeup tests now.

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:24.170
<b>by Keith
You can do it!!
Do your best!
Makeup Tests!</b>

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:24.380
<b>Makeup Tests!
Do your best!
You can do it!!
by Keith</b>

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.590
Begin!

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:27.840
Ah! It's got X and Y!

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.760
Calculate the following formulas.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:29.800
Ah! It's got X and Y!

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:33.930
I can do this one! Armin taught me how to do it!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.980
Hm? Wait a second.

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:40.520
Steak and curry are good, but Hamburg steak
and melon sound good, too.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:45.280
But cake, sushi, bean-paste bun,
ramen, and gyoza are hard to give up, too.

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:50.240
What shall I eat today?

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.330
After all, Sasha flunked the makeup tests, too,

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:55.120
and she now has to take refresher classes.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:56.960
In the meantime...

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.300
Yahoo!

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.380
Hange! This is dangerous!

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:09.050
Conny forgot about the makeup tests,

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.720
so he was automatically
put in refresher classes.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.680
Summer is here.

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:22.440
<i>The time to fight back has come,</i>
<i>climb over that wall</i>

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:28.200
<i>Like a lighthouse, ignite the light of hope</i>

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:33.700
<i>That enormous strength is precisely</i>
<i>what leads the way to freedom</i>

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:39.420
<i>Let's look beyond this conflict, Ausfall!</i>

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:54.510
<i>Inside the wall, with no place to run,</i>

00:15:54.720 --> 00:16:00.190
<i>we're stuck in restrictions and exploits</i>

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:04.730
<i>Even if our glory days of youth</i>
<i>get trampled upon,</i>

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:10.360
<i>I want to at least hold on to the future</i>

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:16.240
<i>I won't give in to that</i>
<i>absurd scolding voice, either</i>

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:21.960
<i>I pledged to the earth that I'd make</i>
<i>our dreams and hopes come true</i>

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:27.340
<i>The time to fight back has come,</i>
<i>the blood in my veins calls forth the future</i>

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:33.140
<i>We'll pull apart all those troublesome rules</i>

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:38.600
<i>Now's the time to raise the flag</i>
<i>of revolt upon that steep wall</i>

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:44.230
<i>Seek prosperity, Ausfall!</i>

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.400
I wanna be popular with girls...

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:54.070
On that day, Jean, who dreams of a sweet,
sugary life but isn't so popular,

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.990
found something in his shoe locker.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:17:00.000
Love Letter! Titan Junior High School
